{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/760084-home-rules-and-meta-gaming","id":760084,"title":"Home Rules and Meta-Gaming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-07T11:09:06-08:00","id":760084,"title":"Home Rules and Meta-Gaming","content":"Has anyone else taken a look at a canon rule or story and just ignored and/or completely rewrote it whenever it came up in a campaign? Not to nock the developers, cWOD is a beautiful game, but we all seen some rules we didn't agree with.<br /> <br /> For example when I saw the whole Samuel Height..... thing, I rewrote the character and skin-dancers as a whole to what I felt hit closer to the message the first author was trying to evoke before...... well Samuel Height happened. With Samuel being an embittered kinfolk, unhappy with the fact his kin were second class citizens in the best of times(and extra breeding material in the worst) while werewolves bathed in the blessings of Gaia. In his attempts to gain equality, demanding the kinfolk be allowed renown among Garou, he was expelled as a nuisance and turned to the call of the wyrm for revenge.<br /> <br /> (Insert events that drove him to becoming an independent ghoul and developing the ritual of rebirth)<br /> <br /> Now we have skindancers, a society of werewolf hunters who strive to assimilate every kinfolk in the world. Each, while lacking the garou's natural regeneration and gaining half as much renown, also lack the aversion to vitae, can learn up to three dots in disciplines, and can hold up to the garou limit of vitae(25 with proper training as per ghoul the addiction rules). Each acting as mercenaries for hire to any vampire with enough vitae.(side note: an embraced skindancer would lose the benifits of the rite of sacred rebirth and thus become a normal vamp)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T12:11:08-08:00","id":760132,"title":"","content":"Well for my setting i rewrote Samuel height as Glass Walker kinfolk because of the tribe`s kinfolk problem with them seem more logical than a CoG.<br /> <br /> I made Silver Fang houses gift available to all the tribe because as houses are for continent mostly it was needless restriction that never came up in game.<br /> <br /> I change the SFs spirits as spouting the ideals of the tribe instead of imposing its degeneration.<br /> <br /> Assigned gift/ritual to certain camps, example: Imminent strike got the same ritual than Dies Ultimae.<br /> <br /> Removed the Stargazers from the setting, they are problematic nobody plays them for the tribe ideals only for the kalindo in my experience so i put kalindo available to everyone.<br /> <br /> And Garous can forge klaives because the explanation in setting didn't made sense to me. So klaive smiting is done with kinfolk because of the silver even though homid garous aren't affected in any way by silver in homid. And if a blacksmith is burning himself with molten silver then he has way WAY worse problems than being a garou or not.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T18:19:36-08:00","id":760384,"title":"","content":"^I personally took away the silver resistance in homid thing, but I think molten silver isn't the only hazard when crafting with the stuff. They did mention in the books that Klaives have to be kept &quot;alive&quot; during the smithing process which makes forging one exceedingly difficult even to the well trained, so it probably can't be melted and poured into a mold the conventional way without &quot;killing&quot; the spirit inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T19:35:39-08:00","id":760413,"title":"","content":"Had a player I tried introducing to the setting... who was too lazy or cheap to buy the books... herself<br /> <br /> After a bit she glanced through them and decided she REALLY disapproved of the material... and insisted it would be easy to change the cosmology... with it just being the two of us<br /> <br /> and was surprirsed I'd hear NOTHING of it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T19:59:29-08:00","id":760431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/760084-home-rules-and-meta-gaming?p=760384#post760384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^I personally took away the silver resistance in homid thing, but I think molten silver isn't the only hazard when crafting with the stuff. They did mention in the books that Klaives have to be kept &quot;alive&quot; during the smithing process which makes forging one exceedingly difficult even to the well trained, so it probably can't be melted and poured into a mold the conventional way without &quot;killing&quot; the spirit inside.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahh i though that it was a rules-with-setting houserules thread.<br /> <br /> In that case yes, i stole rule from forsaken into the game to make it more smooth. Silver hit in all forms but only when it draw blood.<br /> <br /> There is no shapeshifting roll, and each form has the special bonus of forsaken 2ed (except Crinos).<br /> <br /> Regeneration is 1 bashing per turn or 1 lethal per turn if gnosis is spent. <br /> <br /> Purebreed is only a vague stat that has no impact mechanically except in certain specific situations (Only to get entrance into a tribe and dealing with kinfolk of the same tribe)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T02:37:50-08:00","id":760578,"title":"","content":"I haven't really run a game proper myself, but I have few ideas;<br /> <br /> The Gnosis spread being 2/3/4, rather than 1/3/5.<br /> <br /> The city having random serious Wyrm taint, and so every time a character buys anything from a store, there is a roll to see if they get a tainted item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T04:17:25-08:00","id":760601,"title":"","content":"I think I'd get rid of the disparity in starting rage, gnosis, and willpower - give everyone 4 or 5 in each instead of variation based on auspice, breed, and tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T04:45:04-08:00","id":760607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/760084-home-rules-and-meta-gaming?p=760601#post760601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'd get rid of the disparity in starting rage, gnosis, and willpower - give everyone 4 or 5 in each instead of variation based on auspice, breed, and tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in, let people choose how'd they spent the points? Yeah, that's another good way to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T05:03:11-08:00","id":760610,"title":"","content":"That would be interesting - give everyone like 10 points combined to spend as they wish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T04:05:40-08:00","id":761355,"title":"","content":"Created a whole new experience buy system for character creation (there is a post for that somewhere).<br /> <br /> Animal spirits are, like in some umbra descriptions, embodiments of something, that are present in areas where many of these animals live in the material world. They aren't animal wraiths like the animal spirit entry suggests.<br /> <br /> All camps that don't have a strict organization are downgraded to philosophies. All camp gifts are never favoured gifts to characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T07:20:57-08:00","id":761465,"title":"","content":"This is a REALLY minor one, but I do feel strongly about it.<br /> <br /> Garou typically do not have pets. Some animals tied to their totems, like Silver Fang with a trained hunting Falcon or horses for moving, yes. But dogs and cats and others, nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T07:25:49-08:00","id":761473,"title":"","content":"I agree. Although &quot;Silver Crown&quot; has horses for the Silver Fangs and Back Furies have a horse related gift I always found that stupid, especially since lupus form is fast and described as not leading to any exhaustion.<br /> With the Curse also affecting animals gifts like &quot;King of the Beast&quot; become kind of pointless...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T07:33:47-08:00","id":761484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/760084-home-rules-and-meta-gaming?p=761473#post761473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. Although &quot;Silver Crown&quot; has horses for the Silver Fangs and Back Furies have a horse related gift I always found that stupid, especially since lupus form is fast and described as not leading to any exhaustion.<br /> With the Curse also affecting animals gifts like &quot;King of the Beast&quot; become kind of pointless...</div> </div> </div> </div>Horse culture I can understand, given how important they were in ages past to humans. But what does it tell the lupus when you start telling about your dog? XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T07:38:56-08:00","id":761491,"title":"","content":"Didn't Silver Crown also point out how uncomfortable both horse and rider were, and the mounted SF guard only stayed on his horse because the king insisted on it?<br /> About dogs - in one game an NPC who couldn't care less randomly gave my character a puppy from his hunting dog kennel. The group dissolved before anything more could become of it, but theoretically, could that dog turn into a pet or would dominance fights ruin everything at some point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T07:48:30-08:00","id":761500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taci</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/760084-home-rules-and-meta-gaming?p=761491#post761491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Silver Crown also point out how uncomfortable both horse and rider were, and the mounted SF guard only stayed on his horse because the king insisted on it?<br /> About dogs - in one game an NPC who couldn't care less randomly gave my character a puppy from his hunting dog kennel. The group dissolved before anything more could become of it, but theoretically, could that dog turn into a pet or would dominance fights ruin everything at some point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given it was a hunting dog, aka possibly a large-ish dog with a prey-drive, I'd say it would have been very hard. First of all, the character smells like a wolf if they shift with any frequenct. They'd leave hairs and scents on themselves. The dog would be uncomfortable and confused just by the smells. Rage adds to it, it tells the dog the person is -dangerous- and predator.<br /> <br /> I think a dog COULD get used to it, highly depending on the breed of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T11:03:08-08:00","id":761608,"title":"","content":"Um. Smell of Man makes all trained beasts love, obey and like the Homids. So pets and animal companions aren't that hard to pull off, if a bit anachronistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T14:13:24-08:00","id":761704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/760084-home-rules-and-meta-gaming?p=761500#post761500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a dog COULD get used to it, highly depending on the breed of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine that ancient breed dogs with a lot of similarity to wolves, like the snow dogs (huskies, malamutes, samoyeds), akitas, and chow chows would have an easier time with it. They might perceive werewolves as alphas of their own pack.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T18:36:52-08:00","id":761913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/760084-home-rules-and-meta-gaming?p=760132#post760132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Garous can forge klaives because the explanation in setting didn't made sense to me. So klaive smiting is done with kinfolk because of the silver even though homid garous aren't affected in any way by silver in homid. And if a blacksmith is burning himself with molten silver then he has way WAY worse problems than being a garou or not.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's the matter of silver causing Gnosis loss though. W20 tells us that homid are immune even to Gnosis loss in breed form, but I don't know if that was always the case. A homid blacksmith would be at one point less of Gnosis every day that he worked on the blade.<br /> <br /> Regarding rules I think the elephant in the room is the primacy of Rage action over eveyrthing else; it makes combat stupidly fast and deadly for the side that has access to less actions. Particularly screwed this way are spirits, who for all their fancy powers have very little chances of surviving one round of contact with a single werewolves. (Unless you use the Revised ruling that the difficulty to damage a spirit is its Rage, which makes most of the spirit antagonists absurdly hard to dent)<br /> <br /> So I decided that some spirits have access to a charm that lets them spend Essence once per scene to bank on a number of extra actions based on their Rage, to spend during the scene. I don't remember the details but it worked well and spirits were actually a threat again.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T03:30:13-08:00","id":762148,"title":"","content":"I think the uneasiness with silver for a homid smith was due to the reduced frenzy difficulty when near to silver, not necessarily the gnosis penalty. I was kin of pissed, when I read the passage in W20, for I didn't know it from any LARP game I knew, but I was made aware that it had been there in revised, too. I checked and it was, so I stated it as a cross reference problem during open development, that it is mentioned with the homid entry, but not the silver/gnosis entry in revised. But it wasn't fixed.<br /> <br /> I agree that extra actions are broken and Rage makes them too available. The new Dark Age Rules seriously limit the effectiveness of multiple actions and I'd like to see something done along that line with rage, too. Spend one Rage to reduce the multiple action penalties on permanent rage actions, with no more than one attack action per uneven dot or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T03:46:45-08:00","id":762162,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to conceptualize DA-style multiple actions for Werewolf. I kind of think that every Rage-supplied action should be a possible attack action, rather than half of them, because of what Rage represents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T04:55:59-08:00","id":762201,"title":"","content":"Sure, it fits thematically, but the advantage is too high - and the game benefit to experience cost trade off is also too high.<br /> <br /> The benchmark I usually use are the gurahl. In open dev I suggested their bonuses should at least last permanent rage rounds instead of one. Gurahl and garou should have been on par in the War of Rage, garou having the upper hand being in packs.<br /> For a gurahl a point of rage is 1 point of strength or stamina for 1 to 10 rounds. For a garou a point of rage is a minimum of 6 damage dice (1 base, 4 crinos mod, 1 claw damage) with an average of 3 damage, right this turn. So the gurahl with rage 6 has the same trade-off (6 dice of damage) spread over 6 turns while the garou can use them right now.<br /> When spending two rage the discrepancy only increases.<br /> Basically, additional actions are are usually a bonus that can not be compensated by other bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T05:07:15-08:00","id":762206,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the Gurahl could use a house rule too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T05:23:54-08:00","id":762215,"title":"","content":"Well, W20 CBs Gurahl is an improvement to every version before. But just like pimping &quot;Razor Claws&quot;, which had a bad trade-off to additional actions. Increasing the damage bonus and breaking the &quot;damage is rolled against 6&quot; standard was in my opinion the wrong way to fix the huge trade-off that are additional actions. Also, it left revised gifts like Iron Claws, Falcon's Claws and possibly others unadjusted and weak compared to razor claws.<br /> Well, everything that should get better in Werewolf IV or WoD IV - I hope...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T08:15:01-08:00","id":762333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/760084-home-rules-and-meta-gaming?p=762148#post762148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the uneasiness with silver for a homid smith was due to the reduced frenzy difficulty when near to silver, not necessarily the gnosis penalty. I was kin of pissed, when I read the passage in W20, for I didn't know it from any LARP game I knew, but I was made aware that it had been there in revised, too. I checked and it was, so I stated it as a cross reference problem during open development, that it is mentioned with the homid entry, but not the silver/gnosis entry in revised. But it wasn't fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either way i didnt make much sense to me and so it was discarded in my houserules.<br /> <br /> I forgot another one.<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers dont have auspice gifts nor auspice as they rip them off when they dance the spiral. Something i quite like from the pure that they look wrong on the umbra.<br /> <br /> That and to press the idea that to make them weaker but pressing more on the fact that BSDs win by sheer number more than numbers+power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T10:32:20-08:00","id":762401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/760084-home-rules-and-meta-gaming?p=762206#post762206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like the Gurahl could use a house rule too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've usually just ruled that the Gurahl boosts last the scene and it has generally worked out fine. Since they are slower to get Rage back it has tended to balance out fine. I will have to check and see what changes W20 made to them. I have the books, but haven't thoroughly read through them since my group isn't/hasn't been interesting in playing Werewolf these last couple of years. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/760084-home-rules-and-meta-gaming?p=762333#post762333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot another one.<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers dont have auspice gifts nor auspice as they rip them off when they dance the spiral. Something i quite like from the pure that they look wrong on the umbra.<br /> <br /> That and to press the idea that to make them weaker but pressing more on the fact that BSDs win by sheer number more than numbers+power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting this comment by saying, whatever works for your games is awesome for you. That being said, I'm not a fan of weakening the Spirals. They are supposed to be the Garou's equals thematically, and making them weaker versions that just have numbers going for them doesn't sit right in my mind.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}